 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met: three of the five cases were confirmed, on three different scenes. They are 12855a41 with the lead car at 0.75x speed and no time shift (S21), 09a95ffa at 0.75x and no time shift (S12), and 19f339ba with the lead car 0.5 s earlier at 1.25x (S24). All three were run with 200 ms of planner delay. None of these failures was the policy rear-ending the lead car. In every run the ego slowed and drifted left, then hit or was sideswiped by a car in the left lane. In the 19f339ba and 12855a41 runs, nothing was close ahead in the ego's own lane. Every run in the study used 200 ms of delay, so we can't say whether the retiming alone, at zero delay, causes any failure. One of the failures at S12 was a replayed car hitting the ego, and the triage could not say whether the policy was at fault, so that confirmation is a little weaker than it looks.",
